Exercise 4: Reflect on Your Dataset and Transformations
Why normalization is important: Pretrained networks (like ResNet) were trained on ImageNet images that were standardized using specific mean and standard deviation values. Normalizing input data using these same statistics ensures feature activations align with expected distributions and accelerates gradient descent convergence.

Benefits of resizing to (224, 224): Standardizes tensor dimensions so that batch operations can be performed efficiently in PyTorch, matching the input spatial size expected by pre-trained CNN architectures.

Varying input sizes: Convolutional layers can process varying spatial dimensions, but fully connected linear layers require fixed-length inputs. Unequal image sizes prevent tensor batching without custom dynamic padding or spatial pyramid pooling.

