Exercise 8: Analyze Training Configuration
Purpose of choosing specific epoch counts: Prevents underfitting (stopping before convergence) and overfitting (training too long after optimal validation performance is achieved).

Importance of batch size: Larger batch sizes provide smoother gradient updates and leverage parallel hardware better, while smaller batch sizes introduce regularizing noise and reduce memory consumption.

Learning rate scheduler benefit: Dynamic learning rates help escape saddle points early in training and refine step sizes as the optimizer approaches a local minimum.

